# Data Management

Always validate or download before analysis. Preview destructive work with `--dry-run`.

Read `ReadMeDocs/FILE_MANAGEMENT_GUIDE.md` and skill `data-lifecycle`.

## Layout

- `football-data/` — raw league CSVs from football-data.co.uk (`E0_2425.csv`)
- `data/analysis/` — suggestions + `todays_fixtures_YYYYMMDD.json`
- `data/raw/` — upcoming match JSON
- `data/corners/` — corner outputs
- `data/team_stats/` — strength matrices
- `data/archive/` — files older than 7 days
- `data/MANIFEST.json` — inventory

## Canonical commands

```bash
python cli.py --task download --leagues E0,SP1 --season AUTO
python cli.py --task download-fixtures --update-today
python cli.py --task convert-upcoming --file data/raw/upcomingMatches.json --output-dir data/analysis
python cli.py --task validate --check-all
python cli.py --task organize
python src/data_manager.py --full-cleanup --dry-run
python src/data_manager.py --manifest
```

Do not write outside `data/`, `football-data/`, `logs/`, and `models/` unless the user asks.
